Single-database Alembic configuration.

Legacy baseline bootstrap
-------------------------

Revisions 001-006 were written after part of the application schema already
existed, so they are not a complete from-zero baseline. Startup therefore uses
`app.backend_pre_start.bootstrap_legacy_empty_database` as a narrow transition:

* only a database with no `alembic_version` and no business tables is eligible;
* the current SQLAlchemy and SQLModel metadata is created on that same database
  connection and then stamped to the current head;
* every non-empty database runs normal `alembic upgrade head` and is never
  stamped past unapplied revisions.

This bridge is for reproducible competition/local deployment. It is not a
replacement for a future full baseline migration generated and reviewed from
the complete current schema.
